# environment files (secrets) — .env.example is the committed template
**/.env

# The content/version server lives in its own repo (Arsen27/dmv-server);
# server/ here is its working copy. Course content is generated into it by
# `npm run course:export-server`, then committed from inside server/.
/server/

# The authoring toolchain — the admin panel, the course builders and their
# docs — used to be ignored as side tools. It is the main asset now, and it
# existed in exactly one copy, on one disk, until this was written down. So
# admin/, scripts/ and docs/ are tracked, where they already sit: the builder
# addresses everything by relative path, and moving a directory would break it.
# admin/node_modules and admin/.smoke stay out through admin/.gitignore.

# Course material: everything under courses/ is out by default and the two
# packages the builder actually reads are named back in. The default is
# "ignore" on purpose — courses/ is also where 500+ MB of competitor course
# material and every superseded dated handoff snapshot land. Nothing rebuilds
# from those, and a blocklist would only hold until the next directory
# appeared.
/courses/*
!/courses/skeleton/
!/courses/states/

# Local working materials that are nobody's source.
/_to_delete/
/design_handoff_dmv_prep_glass/
/*_Integration_Handoff_*/

# An archive is never a source: each of these is a snapshot of something that
# is either tracked above or deliberately not.
*.zip

# Course packages built for the content server; pushed, not committed.
/out/
